        "id": "condition-2",
        "verificationStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-ver-status",
              "code": "provisional"
            }
          ]
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Personality disorder, likely cluster B / borderline personality disorder traits"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gambling frequency, setting, and course"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Works in a pub gaming room with easy access. Uses electronic gaming machines most days, mainly at his own venue and sometimes at a nearby club; also sometimes bets on online sports late at night. Gambling has continued for at least 12 months and worsened after COVID reopening."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gambling-related preoccupation and impaired control"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports thinking about which machine is due even at dinner with his mother. Plans to spend $50 and be home by 9 pm but stays for hours and spends a few hundred dollars. Reports approximately $1,200 spent over three nights last week and a belief that one good night will fix his financial situation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gambling-related harms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Behind on credit card and Afterpay payments and has a small personal loan. Reports increased conflict with his ex-partner regarding child support and that his mother is concerned about money. Has stopped going to the gym and fishing, preferring to keep money for gambling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Brief problem gambling screen"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Both questions positive; screen indicated probable gambling disorder."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Problem Gambling Severity Index (PGSI)"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Not completed because of time and the patient's tangential history."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood, anxiety, and suicide risk"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mood described as flat and stressed in relation to gambling losses and debt; no persistent low mood or anhedonia outside the gambling context. Anxiety mainly relates to money worries and insomnia after losses; no panic. Denies current suicidal ideation or plan. Occasionally thinks it would be easier to disappear, but denies intent. Protective factors reported: daughter and close relationship with his mother."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Alcohol use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports 3–4 beers after late shifts and 6–7 beers on pay nights. Denies morning drinking and reports no blackouts."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Other drug use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports no other drug use."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Sleep is poor; uses his phone and bets late at night until 2–3 am, with insomnia after losses."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Psychiatric history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports past psychiatric contact in his 20s after a major work-related outburst in which he smashed a glass. He says he was told he had a personality disorder, 'kind of borderline', and describes impulsivity and reacting strongly when people upset him. Previously attended some DBT groups, then stopped. No current psychiatric care or medication and no past psychiatric admissions."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental status examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Tangential but cooperative and mildly fidgety. Speech increased when discussing gambling. Mood described as 'stressed, bit ashamed'; affect congruent. No psychosis. Insight fair regarding gambling; judgement impaired around chasing losses."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
